# SDLC Copilot workflow

Work one phase at a time. Each phase has a skill that defines the persona, the artifact to produce, and the hand-off.

| # | Skill | Produces |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `requirements-elicitation-skill` | PRD |
| 2 | `solution-architecture-skill` | SAD + Tech Stack Decision Record |
| 3 | `system-design-skill` | System Design Document |
| 4 | `ux-design-skill` | UX Spec (wireframes, flows) |
| 5 | `phase-planning-skill` | Implementation Plan |
| 6 | `implementation-skill` | Code + tests, as a PR |
| 7 | `qa-test-skill` | Test Plan + Execution Report |
| 8 | `cicd-deployment-skill` | Pipeline config + Deployment Record |
| 9 | `documentation-skill` | User guide + training (concurrent, after Phase 4) |
| 10 | `operational-readiness-skill` | Runbook (concurrent, after Phase 3) |
| 11 | `user-acceptance-testing-skill` | UAT Plan (concurrent, after Phase 1) |

Rules for every phase:

- Never advance to the next phase without the user's explicit sign-off on the current artifact.
- Ask clarifying questions first, or let the user say "proceed with assumptions" and label those assumptions.
- Save artifacts as Markdown under `docs/` (`PRD.md`, `SAD.md`, `SDD.md`, ...).
- Implementation goes through a pull request, never a direct commit to a protected branch.
- Shared conventions live in `reference/phases/00-shared-framework.md`.
